    "source": "Brain/Nutrition/Vitamins and Minerals.md",
    "contentHtml": "<h1>Vitamins and Minerals</h1>\n<p>Good forms vs toxic forms, plus preservative research. The backbone of [[PawGrade]]&#39;s flagged-ingredient list and [[Scoring System]]. Part of [[Nutrition]].</p>\n<h2>The pattern</h2>\n<p><strong>Inorganic = bad</strong> (sulfates, oxides, selenite → poor absorption, accumulation). <strong>Organic / chelated = good</strong> (proteinate, chelate, methionine → self-regulated, safer).</p>\n<h2>AVOID (toxic / accumulate / poor bioavailability)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Ingredient</th>\n<th>Problem</th>\n<th>Better form</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Menadione</strong> (synthetic K3)</td>\n<td>Depletes glutathione, damages liver cells &amp; RBCs, hemolytic anemia</td>\n<td>Natural K1 (plants), K2 (animal)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sodium selenite</strong></td>\n<td>Free radicals, progressive kidney tubule damage</td>\n<td>Selenomethionine</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Copper sulfate</strong></td>\n<td>Silently accumulates in liver → chronic hepatitis (Labs, Dobermans)</td>\n<td>Copper proteinate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cholecalciferol</strong> (synthetic D3)</td>\n<td>Narrowest safe range of any nutrient; FDA recalls, kidney failure</td>\n<td>Whole-food D (fish, egg yolk)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Zinc oxide</strong></td>\n<td>Poorly absorbed; hemolytic anemia (Huskies/Malamutes)</td>\n<td>Zinc proteinate</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ferric oxide</strong></td>\n<td>Unabsorbable colorant, zero nutrition</td>\n<td>Remove it</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2>CAUTION (poor forms / accumulate)</h2>\n<p>Retinyl palmitate/acetate (synthetic A, liver buildup) · Pyridoxine HCl (B6, chronic excess → neuropathy) · Cyanocobalamin (B12, trace cyanide → use methylcobalamin) · Zinc sulfate · <strong>dl-alpha tocopherol</strong> (synthetic E — natural is <strong>d</strong>-alpha, no &quot;l&quot;).</p>\n<h2>Preservatives (research-backed)</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Ingredient</th>\n<th>Severity</th>\n<th>Note</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>BHA</strong></td>\n<td>Severe</td>\n<td>NTP: squamous tumors; IARC 2B; Prop 65 listed</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>BHT</strong></td>\n<td>Severe</td>\n<td>Liver hypertrophy; inhibits thyroid peroxidase; tumor promoter</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ethoxyquin</strong></td>\n<td>Toxic</td>\n<td>Originally a pesticide; liver/kidney lesions, immune dysfunction; banned in human food many places</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>TBHQ</strong></td>\n<td>Severe</td>\n<td>Immune concerns, tumors at high doses</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Sodium nitrite</strong></td>\n<td>Severe</td>\n<td>Forms nitrosamines → cancer risk</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>See also [[Organs and Lipoma Diet]] for which whole foods supply these nutrients naturally.</p>\n"
