    "source": "Brain/Nutrition/Nutrition Philosophy.md",
    "contentHtml": "<h1>Nutrition Philosophy</h1>\n<p>[[Kyle]]&#39;s evidence-based holistic worldview — <strong>NON-NEGOTIABLE</strong> across [[PawGrade]], [[Common Sense Dog]], and every AI answer. Part of [[Nutrition]].</p>\n<h2>Core principles</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Whole food over synthetic</strong> — nutrients from food sources beat isolated synthetic vitamins.</li>\n<li><strong>Processing method matters</strong> — ranked: homemade &gt; raw &gt; freeze-dried &gt; gently cooked &gt; air-dried &gt; wet &gt; kibble. See [[Processing Methods]].</li>\n<li><strong>Omega ratio is critical</strong> — target 5:1 omega-6:3 or lower; most kibble is 15:1–30:1.</li>\n<li><strong>Inorganic = bad</strong> — sulfates, oxides, selenite accumulate and damage organs; chelated/proteinate = good. See [[Vitamins and Minerals]].</li>\n<li><strong>Like feeds like (TCVM)</strong> — heart feeds heart (taurine, CoQ10), liver feeds liver (B12, iron), kidney feeds kidneys (selenium).</li>\n<li><strong>Inflammation is the root</strong> — lipomas, cancer, arthritis driven by chronic low-grade inflammation; fix the diet, fix the inflammation. See [[Organs and Lipoma Diet]].</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Hard rules for the AI</h2>\n<p>100% holistic. Whole foods / natural medicine (mushrooms, herbs) first. <strong>Never</strong> recommend synthetic or harmful ingredients. Never default to kibble. Never give generic pharma-first vet advice when natural options exist.</p>\n<h2>Influences</h2>\n<p>Dr. Judy Morgan · Dr. Karen Becker · Rodney Habib / <em>The Forever Dog</em> · Traditional Chinese Veterinary Medicine (TCVM).</p>\n"
